/**
\mainpage Bond C++ API

Bond is a small C-like scripting language. This is the API of its compiler, virtual machine and
runtime library.

\section text_encoding Text encoding

All text in Bond is encoded in UTF-8. Every `const char *` that crosses the C++ API is UTF-8,
including:

- Bond source code passed to the Lexer, and strings in Bond scripts and CBO files.
- File names passed to stream factories, StdioFileHandle and the other I/O classes. On Windows,
  they are converted to UTF-16 to open the file, so a name that is not valid UTF-8 fails to open.
  An embedder must not pass names in the ANSI code page.
- Names of functions, structs and other symbols, such as those passed to VM::CallFunction.
- Command line arguments, which the Bond tools obtain with CommandLineArgs.

A Bond `char` holds one byte, which is one UTF-8 code unit rather than one character. Compiler
error columns count code points.
*/
